<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34420" root="فل" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِلٌّ</span></b>  Land <i>in which is no herbage;</i> (K;) or land
<i>not rained upon, and in which is no herbage.</i> (S,
O.) See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَلٌّ</span>, in three places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَدَا فِلًّا مِنَ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الطَّعَامِ</span>, with kesr, means [<i>He went forth early in
the morning</i>] <i>devoid of food.</i> (O.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِلٌّ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِنَ الخَيْرِ</span> occurs in a verse, (S, O,) in the poetry
of 'Abd-Allah Ibn-Rawáhah and in that of
Hassán, (S, O,) meaning <i>Devoid of good.</i> (S,
TA.) [See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلٌّ</span>.] ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  And <i>Such as has become
thin,</i> of hair. (K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُلٌّ</span>.

